course: dictionary
lesson: 7912
title: Reading clues in a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rattlesnake is a snake with a rattle at the end of its tail. Its name gives you clues: "rattle" is a noisy shaking sound, and "snake" is a long animal with no legs. Put them together and you can guess what the animal does.
explain: «A rattlesnake's rattle is made of hollow rings of hard skin» tells you what a rattle looks like. The clue words "hollow" and "hard" help you picture it.
explain: Check your guess by putting it into the sentence. «A rattlesnake buzzes its rattle» makes sense if a rattle is a noisy shake, so your meaning fits.
fact: A rattlesnake is a poisonous (venomous) snake of North and South America.
fact: Its rattle is a stack of hard, hollow rings at the end of its tail.
fact: It shakes the rattle to make a buzzing warning noise, which means "I am dangerous, go away."
fact: It adds a ring each time it sheds its skin, but old rings break off, so you cannot tell its age by counting them.
fact: If you hear a rattle, freeze, find the snake, and back away slowly. Never pick up a snake.
exercise: «A cobra spreads its hood, a rattlesnake buzzes its rattle.» What is the rattle for? | To catch food for dinner | To wave hello to friends | *To give a warning that says stay away | To keep the snake warm
exercise: Where do rattlesnakes live? | *North and South America | Australia only | Only in Europe | Africa and Asia
exercise: What is a rattlesnake's rattle made of? | *Hard, hollow rings of skin | Glass beads | Soft fur
test: A teenager picked up a rattlesnake and it bit his hand. What is the lesson? | It is safe to touch a rattlesnake | *Never pick up a snake, and keep away from it | Snakes are friendly if you pick them up | Bites never hurt
test: Why can't you tell a rattlesnake's age by counting its rings? | *It adds a ring at each shed, and old rings break off | It has no rings at all | It adds a ring every day | Its rings are always painted on
exam: «Rattler» is an informal name. Which word means the same animal? | Cobra | Python | *Rattlesnake | Mamba
